## Comparison table

| Feature | Cookie | sessionStorage | localStorage |
|---|---|---|---|
| Capacity | ~4 KB | ~5–10 MB | ~5–10 MB |
| Lifetime | Set expiry / session | Tab lifetime | Until cleared |
| Sent to server | Yes (every request) | No | No |
| Accessible from JS | Yes (unless HttpOnly) | Yes | Yes |
| Scope | Domain + path | Tab + origin | Origin |
| Shared across tabs | Yes | No | Yes |

## Cookie usage

```js
// Set a cookie (expires in 7 days)
document.cookie = 'token=abc123; max-age=604800; path=/; Secure; SameSite=Strict';

// Read cookies
console.log(document.cookie); // 'token=abc123'

// Best practice: server sets HttpOnly + Secure cookies for auth
// Set-Cookie: token=abc; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict
```

## sessionStorage

```js
// Persist draft form data within the tab
sessionStorage.setItem('draft', JSON.stringify({ title: 'Hello' }));
const draft = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('draft') ?? 'null');

// Auto-cleared when tab closes — no cleanup needed
```

## localStorage

```js
// Persist user theme preference across sessions
localStorage.setItem('theme', 'dark');
const theme = localStorage.getItem('theme') ?? 'light';

// Explicit removal
localStorage.removeItem('theme');
localStorage.clear(); // removes everything
```

## Security note

localStorage and sessionStorage are accessible to any JavaScript on the page — including injected scripts via XSS. Never store JWTs or sensitive auth tokens in either. Prefer `HttpOnly` cookies for authentication.

