## localStorage

```js
// Set
localStorage.setItem('theme', 'dark');
localStorage.setItem('user', JSON.stringify({ id: 1, name: 'Aaron' }));

// Get
const theme = localStorage.getItem('theme'); // 'dark'
const user  = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('user') ?? 'null');

// Remove
localStorage.removeItem('theme');

// Clear all
localStorage.clear();

// Length & iteration
console.log(localStorage.length);
for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
  const key = localStorage.key(i);
  console.log(key, localStorage.getItem(key));
}
```

## sessionStorage

```js
// Same API — but cleared on tab close
sessionStorage.setItem('draft', JSON.stringify({ body: 'Hello' }));
const draft = JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('draft') ?? 'null');
```

## Cross-tab communication via storage event

```js
// In Tab A — writes to localStorage
localStorage.setItem('message', 'hello from tab A');

// In Tab B — listens for changes
window.addEventListener('storage', (e) => {
  console.log(e.key);     // 'message'
  console.log(e.newValue); // 'hello from tab A'
  console.log(e.oldValue); // previous value or null
});
// Note: the tab that set the value does NOT fire its own storage event
```

## Capacity and limitations

- **Synchronous**: blocks the main thread — avoid storing large data (use IndexedDB for blobs/binary)
- **String-only**: `JSON.stringify`/`JSON.parse` for objects
- **Not available in Web Workers or Service Workers**: use IndexedDB there
- **Private browsing**: storage may be isolated or limited
- **Security**: accessible to all scripts on the same origin — never store tokens (use HttpOnly cookies instead)

